{"unit_id":"kenryu42__cc-safety-net#readme-3","repo":"kenryu42/cc-safety-net","commit":"6f34af1f777ba28d331b7809a2bb087a001d353d","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"cc-safety-net README · Introduction：CC Safety Net (Coding CLI Safety Net) blocks destructive commands and access to secrets such as SSH keys and `.env` files before the tool call runs. It parses what the command does. Wrapping the command or reordering flags does not hide it. A broken config file falls back to safe defaults instead of stopping your agent. It is not a sandbox: it does not contain processes, set filesystem permissions, or watch network egress.","source":"extracted","section":"Introduction"}
