{"unit_id":"kenryu42__cc-safety-net#readme-6","repo":"kenryu42/cc-safety-net","commit":"6f34af1f777ba28d331b7809a2bb087a001d353d","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"cc-safety-net README · How it works：<p align=\"center\">\n  <picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"./.github/assets/how-it-works-dark.svg\">\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"./.github/assets/how-it-works-light.svg\">\n    <img alt=\"An AI coding agent tries to run a command or open a file. CC Safety Net checks what it would actually do before it runs. Safe calls such as git status run normally; dangerous ones such as git reset --hard never run, and the agent is told why.\" src=\"./.github/assets/how-it-works-light.svg\" width=\"720\">\n  </picture>\n</p>","source":"extracted","section":"How it works"}
{"unit_id":"kenryu42__cc-safety-net#readme-7","repo":"kenryu42/cc-safety-net","commit":"6f34af1f777ba28d331b7809a2bb087a001d353d","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"cc-safety-net README · Supported coding CLIs：<table align=\"center\">\n  <tr>\n    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/installation/amp-code\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"./.github/assets/amp-dark.svg\"><img alt=\"Amp Code\" src=\"./.github/assets/amp-light.svg\" height=\"32\"></picture><br>Amp Code</a></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/installation/antigravity-cli\"><img alt=\"Antigravity CLI\" src=\"./.github/assets/antigravity-cli.png\" height=\"32\"><br>Antigravity CLI</a></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/installation/claude-code\"><img alt=\"Claude Code\" src=\"./.github/assets/claude-code.svg\" height=\"32\"><br>Claude Code</a></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/installation/codex\"><img alt=\"Codex\" src=\"./.github/assets/codex.svg\" height=\"32\"><br>Codex</a></td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/installation/cursor\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"./.github/assets/cursor-dark.svg\"><img alt=\"Cursor\" src=\"./.github/assets/cursor-light.svg\" height=\"32\"></picture><br>Cursor</a></td>\n    ","source":"extracted","section":"Supported coding CLIs"}
{"unit_id":"kenryu42__cc-safety-net#readme-8","repo":"kenryu42/cc-safety-net","commit":"6f34af1f777ba28d331b7809a2bb087a001d353d","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"cc-safety-net README · Features：- **Blocks destructive commands** such as `git reset --hard`, `git push --force`, and `rm -rf` on dangerous targets, and install scripts piped from the internet (`curl … | bash`), even inside `bash -c` or `python -c`. See [Blocked commands](https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/reference/blocked-commands).\n- **Blocks secret access** to SSH keys, `.env` files, `~/.aws`, and coding-CLI credentials, from the shell and from the agent's file tools. See [Secret protection](https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/reference/secret-protection).\n- **Tunes the policy in a GUI.** Run `npx cc-safety-net gui` to pick the Standard, Strict, or Paranoid preset and turn rules on or off. See [Dashboard](https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/guides/dashboard).\n- **Adds blocks through rulebooks**: official packs for Terraform, AWS, gcloud, and Azure, or your own JSON. See [Official rulebooks](https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/configuration/rulebooks).\n- **Shares policy through git.** Commit `.cc-safety-net/` so clones and cloud sessions get the same rules. See [Team setup](https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/guides/team-setup).\n- **Embeds in your own tools.** Call `checkCommand` from Node.js without installing ","source":"extracted","section":"Features"}
{"unit_id":"kenryu42__cc-safety-net#readme-9","repo":"kenryu42/cc-safety-net","commit":"6f34af1f777ba28d331b7809a2bb087a001d353d","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"cc-safety-net README · Quick start：You need Node.js 22 or higher. Install into the coding CLIs on this machine, then check that protection is working:\n\n```bash\nnpx -y cc-safety-net@latest install\nnpx -y cc-safety-net@latest doctor\n```\n\nUpdate with `npx -y cc-safety-net@latest update` and uninstall with `npx -y cc-safety-net uninstall`. Keep the `@latest` qualifier: a bare `cc-safety-net` spec can run an older copy from the npx cache. Per-CLI requirements are in [Installation](https://ccsafetynet.com/docs/installation).","source":"extracted","section":"Quick start"}
